# .NET build output
bin/
obj/
[Rr]elease/
[Rr]eleases/
*.user
*.suo

# Coverage output (produced by `dotnet test --collect` locally and in CI; never committed)
coverage/
[Cc]overageReport/

# IDEs
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.DS_Store

# AI Tools Ignore List
.cursorindexingignore
.claudeignore
.claude/
.cursor/
CLAUDE.md
TESTING.md
playtest-history/
# Claude Code local worktrees / scratch state -- machine-local, never committed
.claude/worktrees/
# Personal, machine-local permissions/settings (absolute local paths) -- not committed
.claude/settings.local.json

# Vintage Story runtime data (never commit game data or the game itself)
VintagestoryData/
Mods/

# Third-party mod DLLs extracted from the installed LibGUI (`gui`, hard dep) and ConfigLib
# (`configlib`, optional soft dep) mods for Mod.csproj's <Reference> HintPaths -- no usable
# NuGet package exists at the installed versions, so these are vendored locally rather than
# restored via NuGet. See src/Mod/lib/README.md for the exact source .zip/versions and
# re-extraction steps.
src/Mod/lib/*
!src/Mod/lib/README.md

# Art source/backup files under assets/ -- Photoshop sources and "OG"/backup copies of textures
# that would otherwise ship in the public mod zip (build/package.sh blanket-copies src/Mod/assets/).
# Keep them local: only the wired-up final PNGs belong in the release. Covers e.g.
# scribe-sm-OG.png/.psd, sketchbook-mod.psd, *-og.png, and the "lectern (OG)/" backup dir.
*.psd
*-og.png
*-OG.png
*(OG)*

# Local env / secrets
.env
*.local

# Screenshots: not tracked yet (curate and un-ignore selectively later). Scoped to root
# only (leading /) so it doesn't also catch playtest-history/screenshots/ below, which is
# meant to be committed.
/screenshots/
docs/media/screenshots/

# Playtest checklist submissions (app lives in the separate vs-playtest-checklist repo):
# ephemeral local reports queued for Claude to review, not meant to be committed
.playtest-submissions/

# LibGUI (vslibgui) local references for the explore-libgui-adoption change: the wiki cloned
# to .wiki/ (so `rg <term> ./.wiki/` works verbatim) and the full source to reference/vslibgui/.
# Upstream repos, not ours -- read-only research material, never committed. Re-clone with:
#   git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/ripls56/vslibgui.wiki.git .wiki
#   git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/ripls56/vslibgui.git reference/vslibgui
.wiki/
reference/vslibgui/

# Decompiled dump of our OWN vendored src/Mod/lib/Gui.dll (the shipped binary, more authoritative
# than the vslibgui source above when they disagree) -- derived output, not ours to commit, and
# goes stale whenever Gui.dll is bumped. Regenerate with: build/decompile-libgui.sh
reference/vslibgui-decompiled/

# Atlas (integration-test harness) local references: source + wiki cloned for ground-truth
# lookups when the mods.vintagestory.at page is thin. Upstream repos, not ours -- re-clone with:
#   git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/Pixnop/Atlas.git reference/atlas
#   git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/Pixnop/Atlas.wiki.git reference/atlas-wiki
reference/atlas/
reference/atlas-wiki/

# Seralth's independently-shipped Linux HarfBuzz fix (community corroboration for
# ScribeHarfBuzzLoadFix.cs) -- upstream repo, not ours, kept for local diffing. Re-clone with:
#   git clone --depth 50 https://github.com/Seralth/harfbuzzfix.git reference/harfbuzzfix
reference/harfbuzzfix/

# playtest-history/ is NOT ignored -- it's a curated, committed record of promoted
# playtest screenshots (see vs-playtest-checklist's promote_screenshot.py).

.handoff.md
.auto-resume.md

# Base-game texture copies pulled for local art reference (proprietary; scratch, never committed)
reference/base-game-textures/

# Base-game tablet shape/textures copied as a starting point for custom tablet models
# (proprietary; scratch, never committed)
reference/tablet-model/
reference/tablet-placeholder/

# Base-game oak textures pulled for local art reference (proprietary; scratch, never committed)
reference/oak-textures/

# Unpacked third-party mods used for the fix-carried-notebook-detection investigation
